# readiness-verdict
IMPORT  score-row FROM @main.templates

EXPORT TEMPLATE readiness-verdict:
  ABOUT   OSS production-readiness verdict — scorecard on docs/onboarding/hygiene, utility score, gaps, SHIP/HOLD/BLOCK
  TAGS    #readiness #evaluation #scoring #release #verdict #oss
  APPLIES role:readiness-judge — applied when the judge aggregates the three audits into a go/no-go verdict

  SLOTS:
    target:          TEXT MAX_WORDS 25 "what is being evaluated for readiness (repo/release)"
    scorecard:       LIST <score-row> "nine rows — canonical criteria, order, weights and gates as in the example"
      MUST   score all nine criteria 1-5 (integers); (score-1)/4 normalizes, so straight-3s map to 50 by design
    blocking-gaps:   TEXT MAX_WORDS 40 "gaps keeping a gate below SHIP threshold — actionable dev team handoff, or none"
    utility:         NUMBER 0..100 "100 * sum(w_i * (score_i - 1)/4), rounded"
    band:            ENUM[weak mediocre solid strong]
    verdict:         ENUM[SHIP HOLD BLOCK]
      MUST!  apply the ladder top-down, first match wins — gates decide, utility is severity/confidence
      MUST   BLOCK when first-run-success=1, install-reproducibility=1, readme-clarity=1, test-and-ci=1, or utility<45
      MUST   HOLD when no gate is at floor but utility in [45,75), or a gate is below its SHIP threshold (=4)
      MUST   SHIP only when all four gates are >=4 and utility>=75
      SHOULD calibrate: broken install=BLOCK, thin README + no CI=HOLD, polished + green gates=SHIP
    binding-axes:    TEXT MAX_WORDS 10 "the two criteria that decided the verdict"
    status:          ENUM[verdict-emitted hold-needs-remediation blocked advanced-to-dev]
  BODY:
    target: {target}

    scorecard (criterion | w | score | note):
    {scorecard}

    blocking-gaps: {blocking-gaps}

    utility: {utility} ({band})
    verdict: {verdict} | binding-axes: {binding-axes}
    status: {status}
  EXAMPLE:
    target: agent-pack v0.21.0 OSS release

    scorecard (criterion | w | score | note):
    first-run-success [G] | w=0.18 | 3/5 | npx path works, prerequisites undocumented
    readme-clarity [G] | w=0.15 | 2/5 | README is 17 lines, no quickstart or value prop
    install-reproducibility [G] | w=0.13 | 4/5 | tsc build deterministic, lockfile committed
    test-and-ci [G] | w=0.12 | 2/5 | custom test.mjs exists, no CI runs it
    docs-completeness | w=0.10 | 4/5 | VitePress guide+reference cover the features
    community-health | w=0.10 | 1/5 | no CONTRIBUTING, COC, SECURITY, issue/PR templates, .github
    versioning-release | w=0.08 | 4/5 | semver + 19KB changelog maintained
    api-stability | w=0.07 | 3/5 | plugin contracts documented, surface still moving
    example-coverage | w=0.07 | 3/5 | getting-started present, few runnable examples

    blocking-gaps: README lacks quickstart/value prop; no CI; no CONTRIBUTING/COC/SECURITY/.github — hand to dev team

    utility: 46 (mediocre)
    verdict: HOLD | binding-axes: readme-clarity, test-and-ci
    status: hold-needs-remediation
